{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:2.40.400","page_type":"section"},"citation":"2.40.400","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.400","content_hash":"e0f925cad6f6e21a4fee89e5fb130a5fd65a49dd02075c0f2ff39a574c74f717","heading":"Pleas – Failure to appear.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.400:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.400","text":"(a) A plea of guilty is an admission of the charge and every material fact alleged therein.\n(b) A plea of no contest is a formal declaration that the accused person does not contest the charge. When such a plea is entered, a finding of guilty may be adjudged thereon. The plea cannot be used against the accused person as an admission in any other action based on the same act.\n(c) A plea of not guilty denies and puts into issue every material fact alleged in the charge.\n(d) If the accused person refuses to plead, the court shall enter a plea of not guilty.\n(e) If the accused person fails to appear, the court shall declare the appearance bond to be forfeited and may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused person. (Ord. 20206 § 9, 9-10-19; Ord. 17666 § 42, 3-27-01. Code 1995 § 50-77. Formerly 2.110.400.)\nState Law References: Similar State statute, K.S.A. 12-4406 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"2d3cdc75-03b9-5763-85fb-76452dcbd678"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.400","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.400","content_hash":"67f4ef6ac3577e6c9a48cb1088233b86898bb31ff2f32872b78e590728ac133d","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.400:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_ke